# Legacy scope — ignore by default

Unless the user **@-mentions** a path below in the current message, do **not**:

- read, search, cite, or edit files under `legacy/`
- read, search, cite, or edit files under `tests/legacy_agent/`
- import from `legacy.*` or suggest changes that depend on legacy modules
- treat legacy code or its tests as the source of truth for new work

**Exception:** If the user `@legacy/`, `@tests/legacy_agent/`, or `@`-mentions a specific file inside those trees, work on legacy only for that scoped task.

## Canonical paths (use these instead)

| Area | Use | Not for new work |
|------|-----|------------------|
| Agent graph | `agent/builder.py` (`build_agent`) | `legacy/agent/graph.py` |
| Agent config | `agent/config.py` | legacy agent config |
| Nodes / edges | `agent/core/nodes/`, `agent/core/edges/` | `legacy/agent/nodes.py` |
| Capabilities | `agent/capabilities/` | `legacy/agent/reflection/`, `legacy/agent/subgraph/` |
| Agent tests | `tests/agent/` | `tests/legacy_agent/` |
| RAG | `rag/` | `legacy/_eval_/` (old eval harness) |
| Tools | `tools/` | — |

Public API: `from agent import AgentConfig, build_agent` (`agent/__init__.py`).

## Docs

Design docs under `docs/` may describe superseded layouts (`agent/graph.py`, CRAG subgraph plans, etc.). Prefer **canonical code** above. Only follow a design doc when the user `@`-mentions it or asks to align implementation with that doc.

## When unsure

Search and change code under `agent/`, `rag/`, `tools/`, `tests/agent/` first. Do not pull patterns from `legacy/` to answer general architecture or feature questions.
